rections include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Neurophysiology"},{"text":"M.Sc Clinical Neurophysiology"},{"text":"M.Sc Neuroscience"},{"text":"M.Sc Neurotechnology"},{"text":"M.Sc Medical Technology"},{"text":"Clinical Research"},{"text":"Healthcare Technology"},{"text":"Biomedical Engineering"},{"text":"Healthcare Data Science"},{"text":"Hospital Administration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a student wanting to remain clinically focused, Clinical Neurophysiology/Neurophysiology is generally the most aligned direction."},{"type":"p","text":"For a technology-focused student, Neuroscience + signal processing/AI can create a strong research and industry pathway."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"h","text":"EEG Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Routine EEG"},{"text":"Video EEG"},{"text":"Long-term EEG"},{"text":"Epilepsy monitoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"EMG/NCS Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nerve conduction studies"},{"text":"Electromyography"},{"text":"Peripheral nerve disorders"},{"text":"Neuromuscular investigations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Intraoperative Neurophysiology"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Surgical monitoring"},{"text":"Neural pathway monitoring"},{"text":"Real-time signal changes"},{"text":"Neurosurgical procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neurocritical Care Monitoring"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Continuous EEG"},{"text":"ICU neurological monitoring"},{"text":"Coma monitoring"},{"text":"Seizure detection"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sleep Neurophysiology"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG"},{"text":"Sleep staging"},{"text":"Polysomnography"},{"text":"Sleep-related neurological disorders"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neurotechnology & Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain-computer interfaces"},{"text":"EEG signal processing"},{"text":"Neuro-AI"},{"text":"Computational neuroscience"},{"text":"Brain-signal analytics"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Neuro-Electrophysiology Technology Degree","Clinical Internship","Neurophysiology Technologist","Senior Technologist","EEG / EMG-NCS Specialist","Neurodiagnostic / IONM Specialist","Senior / Lead Neurophysiology","Neurophysiology Lab Coordinator","Clinical / Academic / Technical Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"A parallel technology pathway can develop as:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Neurophysiology Technologist","Neurophysiological Data Analyst","EEG Signal Processing Specialist","Neuro-AI / Neurotechnology Research","Clinical Neurotechnology Specialist"]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should aim to have:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neuroanatomy"},{"text":"Neurophysiology"},{"text":"Neurological conditions"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Patient safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neurodiagnostic"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EEG"},{"text":"10–20 system"},{"text":"EEG montages"},{"text":"Artifact recognition"},{"text":"EMG principles"},{"text":"NCS principles"},{"text":"Evoked potentials"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neurodiagnostic equipment"},{"text":"Digital signal acquisition"},{"text":"Signal processing"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Scientific visualization"},{"text":"Basic machine learning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neurologist communication"},{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Technical documentation"},{"text":"Equipment troubleshooting"},{"text":"Clinical teamwork"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"Neuro-Electrophysiology graduate with strong foundations in neuroanatomy and neurophysiology, hands-on clinical exposure to EEG and neurodiagnostic investigations, understanding of EMG/NCS and evoked-potential techniques, competence in electrode placement and signal-quality management, and foundational skills in digital signal processing and neurodiagnostic technology."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Neuro-Electrophysiology Technology","EEG","EMG/NCS","Evoked Potentials","Neurodiagnostic Equipment","Signal Processing","Clinical Neurophysiology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This pathway is particularly strong for students who want a combination of clinical healthcare, neuroscience, medical technology, and electrophysiological data."},{"type":"note","label":"Database note","text":"“Neurophysiology Technologist” is an appropriate normalized target title. Related titles such as EEG Technologist, Neurodiagnostic Technologist, and Clinical Neurophysiology Technologist may be used by different hospitals and institutions, so these can be retained as alternate job titles in the database."}]}]}